      "instance_name": "shiba_inu_meme_culture",
      "label": "Shiba Inu Meme Culture",
      "description": "The use of the Shiba Inu dog as a visual element in memes is part of internet meme culture. The dog's specific expression (often called 'Shiba Inu face' or 'doge') is frequently used to convey emotions like smugness, confusion, or victimhood. In this context, the dog's expression is leveraged to imply a false sense of victimhood, which is then falsely attributed to Jews in the text.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_d1648784"
